  "defect_repaired": "G-R3-1",
  "reason": "R3.1 repairs G-R3-1: the operationally-spent refusal was keyed only on the whole-matrix terminal proof, so losing or altering a single untracked local binary degraded that proof and re-opened every already-completed cell at the entry gate, letting authorize_cell_execution mint a signed optimizer permit for a cell that had already run. The repair adds a per-cell immutability guard that does not depend on the whole-matrix state. It edits digest-bound source and tests, so the live source digest moves again and the R3 post-execution amendment stops carrying the live binding. This link anchors the new binding and preserves the R3 amendment by exact bytes, so the twelve historical cells, their binaries, the frozen analysis and the grant remain reproducible under the binding they were produced under. It is provenance, not permission.",
